{{- /*
results.html.tmpl — the search-results region. Data: render.ResultsData.

This is a FRAGMENT: no <html>, <head> or <body>. It is rendered two ways and
must be identical in both:

  1. included by search.html.tmpl inside <div id="search-results">
  2. returned on its own by the snippet endpoint /search/results?q=…, which the
     page's JavaScript drops into that same div

Every state ends with a hidden [data-search-status] element carrying
.StatusText. The script copies its text into the page's persistent
role="status" region; the results region itself is not a live region.

"bookmark-item" is defined in list.html.tmpl (all three templates are parsed
into one set), so list pages and search results share one card markup.
See TEMPLATES.md.
*/ -}}
{{- if not .Queried}}
                <div class="cdz-search-empty" data-search-empty>
                    <p class="cdz-search-prompt">Start typing to search…</p>
                    <div hidden data-search-status>{{.StatusText}}</div>
                </div>
{{- else if not .Bookmarks}}
                <div class="cdz-search-noresults">
                    <p class="cdz-search-prompt">No results for &ldquo;{{.Query}}&rdquo;.</p>
                    <p class="cdz-search-hint">Only bookmark titles and site names are searched, and each
                        word has to match from the start of a word &mdash; try a shorter or different term.</p>
                    <div hidden data-search-status>{{.StatusText}}</div>
                </div>
{{- else}}
                <div class="cdz-search-hits">
                    <p class="cdz-search-count">
{{- if .Truncated}}More than {{.Count}} results{{else if eq .Count 1}}1 result{{else}}{{.Count}} results{{end}} for &ldquo;{{.Query}}&rdquo;</p>
                    <ul class="cdz-bm-list">
{{- range .Bookmarks}}
{{template "bookmark-item" .}}
{{- end}}
                    </ul>
{{- if .Truncated}}
                    <p class="cdz-search-truncated">More than 100 matches &mdash; refine your search.</p>
{{- end}}
                    <div hidden data-search-status>{{.StatusText}}</div>
                </div>
{{- end}}
